{
  "id": "spore-scar",
  "title": "Spore-Scar System",
  "thumbnail": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jt1919191919/dnd-tool/refs/heads/main/data/images/d20-placeholder2.jpg",
  "description": "",
  "content": "<div><font color=\"#ffffff\"><br></font></div><div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><h1><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Background Info</font></span></h1><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">You melded spores with something enhanced by Faerzress in the Underdark.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Your spores have a demonic infection.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Every time PCs have gotten scars (from getting KO'd) your spores infected the wounds.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">But your druidic magic is stabilizing everyone as long as they stay close to you.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Skabatha gave you a way to use hag magic to harness these demonic spores into useful abilities.</span></span></li></ul><h1><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Spellcasting Focus&nbsp;</font></span></h1><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">The Cicada Vial itself is a spellcasting focus.&nbsp;</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">This means you can hold it in one hand while casting spells, and it counts as Material Components needed for spells. (remember this does not count for Material Components with gold values)</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Flavor-wise, you temporarily uncork the Vial while casting, letting the spores out to help cast your spell.</span></span></li></ul><h1><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">How to Gain More Envelopes of Cards&nbsp;</font></span></h1><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">During a Long Rest, you spend 2 hours focusing on another PC in the Party.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">You hold up the Cicada Vial and it wiggles in there and the spores it gives off whisper creepy little mutterings only you can hear, telling you its ideas for new deals you can make with someone, the rules of the deals, and the abilities they give.</span></span></li></ul><h1><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">How to Make a Deal and Give Someone a Card</font></span></h1><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">During a Long Rest, you spend 2 hours focusing on the Cicada Vial as it whispers a voice only you can hear.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">If you’re giving </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">yourself </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">a card, you’re making the deal with the creepy voices coming from the Cicada in the Vial.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Keep everything secret from other players! Don’t show them cards! Roleplay it out, describing the ability in-character as if making the deal with the other player.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">PC must have an un-assigned Scar and meet the prerequisites on the card.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">You focus your spores and weave your druidic magic to harness the Demon/Rift powers infused in their scars. The PC then inhales spores from the Vial and permanently gains the new ability.</span></span></li></ul><h1><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">How People Use Their Card</font></span></h1><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">When you or other PCs want to use an ability they gained from a deal card, you must be holding the Cicada Vial like a spell focus.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">You pop the cork momentarily, letting spores out to mingle with infected spores from you or the other PCs.&nbsp;</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">As a Free Action, you must always spend 1 of your Hit Dice. Roll your HD. Rolling a 1 is bad.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Follow the rules on the card.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">FYI, normally HD are used to regain health on Short Rests, and you regain half of your HD rounded down after Long Rests.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Your HD roll cannot be rerolled by Inspiration or anything else.</span></span></li></ul><h1><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Must Use Every Day</font></span></h1><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">You must use the Spore-Scar System at least once per day.&nbsp;</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">This includes either Gaining an Envelope, Making a Deal, or </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline;\">anyone</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"> Using a Card ability.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-e61e2b5c-7fff-fba8-b140-8dd1d15ecc79\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">If you end the day without doing any of those things, you take a Level of Exhaustion which only goes away once you use the System again.</span></span></li></ul></span><!--EndFragment--></div><div><font color=\"#ffffff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ffffff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ffffff\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ffffff\"><br></font></div><div><br></div>",
  "visibleTo": [
    "__ALL__"
  ],
